        "news_site": "ESA",
        "summary": "Homer\u2019s The Odyssey chronicles Odysseus\u2019s journey home to Ithaca after the Trojan War. A distance of approximately 530 km as the crow flies, yet it takes Odysseus ten years and countless adventures to arrive\u2014without his crew or his boat. What could Odysseus\u2019s journey have looked like if he had modern-day satellite navigation systems, such as Galileo, at his disposal?",
